 "pvp_rule": "peaceful",
 "quests": [
  {
   "copper": 38,
   "description": "Out here, a welcoming light can leave you waist-deep in water with someone demanding a toll. Kill six Wandering Wisps after dark in the Whispering Canopy, in the east of Whispering Reedlands. I cannot prove they work for the toll collectors, but the collectors certainly appreciate the business.",
   "giver": "r20_anchor_024_host",
   "giver_name": "Taleko Drycord",
   "giver_settlement": "Whisperreed Landing",
   "id": "whispering_reeds_01",
   "min_level": 20,
   "objectives": [
    "kill 6 wandering_wisp [in kragmar_whispering_reedlands/canopy]"
   ],
   "objectives_raw": [
    {
     "area": "kragmar_whispering_reedlands/canopy",
     "count": 6,
     "mobs": [
      "grug_mobs:wandering_wisp"
     ],
     "type": "kill"
    }
   ],
   "prerequisites": [],
   "reward_items": [],
   "title": "Do Not Follow Every Light",
   "turnin": "r20_anchor_024_host",
   "xp": 405
  },
  {
   "copper": 45,
   "description": "Toll Mirefolk have settled in the Hushwater Nests northeast from here and decided every crossing belongs to them. Kill six before another traveller pays for the same stretch of water twice. I asked who gave them the river; they were strangely unwilling to introduce us.",
   "giver": "r20_anchor_024_host",
   "giver_name": "Taleko Drycord",
   "giver_settlement": "Whisperreed Landing",
   "id": "whispering_reeds_02",
   "min_level": 21,
   "objectives": [
    "kill 6 toll_mirefolk [in kragmar_whispering_reedlands/hushwater_nests]"
   ],
   "objectives_raw": [
    {
     "area": "kragmar_whispering_reedlands/hushwater_nests",
     "count": 6,
     "mobs": [
      "grug_mobs:toll_mirefolk"
     ],
     "type": "kill"
    }
   ],
   "prerequisites": [
    "whispering_reeds_01"
   ],
   "reward_items": [],
   "title": "The Water Signed Nothing",
   "turnin": "r20_anchor_024_host",
   "xp": 473
  },
  {
   "copper": 6,
   "description": "Rain takes the ink from my tallies, but our undead kin seem determined to remember everything. Travel to Ossuary Ledgerstead in Ossuary Reach and speak with Sovel Namekeeper about work. Give my greetings before giving your name, or you may end up filed among the supplies.",
   "giver": "r20_anchor_024_host",
   "giver_name": "Taleko Drycord",
   "giver_settlement": "Whisperreed Landing",
   "id": "whispering_journey_ossuary",
   "min_level": 22,
   "objectives": [
    "talk to Sovel Namekeeper (r20_anchor_020)"
   ],
   "objectives_raw": [
    {
     "count": 1,
     "npc": "r20_anchor_020_host",
     "type": "talk"
    }
   ],
   "prerequisites": [
    "whispering_reeds_01"
   ],
   "reward_items": [],
   "title": "Names That Outlast the Rain",
   "turnin": "r20_anchor_020_host",
   "xp": 70
  },
  {
   "copper": 6,
   "description": "A troll who knows only reeds will try to weave every problem into a basket. Visit Brakka Jarward at Speargrass Wellhold in Speargrass Reach, carry my greetings, and ask what work needs doing. Our orc kin may show you another use for those hands.",
   "giver": "r20_anchor_024_host",
   "giver_name": "Taleko Drycord",
   "giver_settlement": "Whisperreed Landing",
   "id": "whispering_journey_speargrass",
   "min_level": 22,
   "objectives": [
    "talk to Brakka Jarward (r20_anchor_022)"
   ],
   "objectives_raw": [
    {
     "count": 1,
     "npc": "r20_anchor_022_host",
     "type": "talk"
    }
   ],
   "prerequisites": [
    "whispering_reeds_01"
   ],
   "reward_items": [],
   "title": "Where the Reeds Give Way",
   "turnin": "r20_anchor_022_host",
   "xp": 70
  },
  {
   "copper": 38,
   "description": "Two carts and a mule lost, and still somebody says the Reed Crocodiles look like logs. Kill six in the Whispering Mudbanks north from here, where we haul our stone. They wait there day and night; at least one thing around this quarry never misses a shift.",
   "giver": "r20_anchor_066_host",
   "giver_name": "Zali Runoff",
   "giver_settlement": "Reedstone Cut",
   "id": "whispering_cut_01",
   "min_level": 23,
   "objectives": [
    "kill 6 reed_crocodile [in kragmar_whispering_reedlands/mudbanks]"
   ],
   "objectives_raw": [
    {
     "area": "kragmar_whispering_reedlands/mudbanks",
     "count": 6,
     "mobs": [
      "grug_mobs:reed_crocodile"
     ],
     "type": "kill"
    }
   ],
   "prerequisites": [],
   "reward_items": [],
   "title": "That Is No Floating Log",
   "turnin": "r20_anchor_066_host",
   "xp": 450
  },
  {
   "copper": 26,
   "description": "The quarry pumps squeal loud enough to drown out the frogs, and the frogs have put years into that chorus. Bring me two Slime Gel to grease them, taken from the Bubbling Bog Oozes in the Whispering Thicket, in the heart of Whispering Reedlands. The oozes come out there after dark, making considerably less fuss than my machinery.",
   "giver": "r20_anchor_066_host",
   "giver_name": "Zali Runoff",
   "giver_settlement": "Reedstone Cut",
   "id": "whispering_cut_02",
   "min_level": 24,
   "objectives": [
    "bring 2 grug_mobs:slime_gel"
   ],
   "objectives_raw": [
    {
     "count": 2,
     "item": "grug_mobs:slime_gel",
     "type": "item"
    }
   ],
   "prerequisites": [
    "whispering_cut_01"
   ],
   "reward_items": [],
   "title": "Quiet the Pumps",
   "turnin": "r20_anchor_066_host",
   "xp": 310
  },
  {
   "copper": 19,
   "description": "Every flood leaves fresh Reed Crocodiles in the Whispering Mudbanks north from here, and none has offered to pull a cart. Kill six there, by day or night, for this repeatable bounty. It opens again twenty minutes after you turn it in; stone waits patiently, but my haulers should not have to.",
   "giver": "r20_anchor_066_host",
   "giver_name": "Zali Runoff",
   "giver_settlement": "Reedstone Cut",
   "id": "whispering_cut_bounty",
   "min_level": 25,
   "objectives": [
    "kill 6 reed_crocodile [in kragmar_whispering_reedlands/mudbanks]"
   ],
   "objectives_raw": [
    {
     "area": "kragmar_whispering_reedlands/mudbanks",
     "count": 6,
     "mobs": [
      "grug_mobs:reed_crocodile"
     ],
     "type": "kill"
    }
   ],
   "prerequisites": [
    "whispering_cut_02"
   ],
   "reward_items": [],
   "title": "Bounty: Jaws on the Haul Path (repeatable)",
   "turnin": "r20_anchor_066_host",
   "xp": 233
  },
  {
   "copper": 38,
   "description": "Listen to the Whispering Mire Nests southeast from here: the reeds whisper, and the Toll Mirefolk shout over them. Kill six mirefolk there to weaken their tollkeeper's hold on these waters. We have heard quite enough about what we owe for crossing our own home.",
   "giver": "r20_anchor_046_host",
   "giver_name": "Enashi Reedvoice",
   "giver_settlement": "Reedvoice Station",
   "id": "whispering_voice_01",
   "min_level": 27,
   "objectives": [
    "kill 6 toll_mirefolk [in kragmar_whispering_reedlands/mire_nests]"
   ],
   "objectives_raw": [
    {
     "area": "kragmar_whispering_reedlands/mire_nests",
     "count": 6,
     "mobs": [
      "grug_mobs:toll_mirefolk"
     ],
     "type": "kill"
    }
   ],
   "prerequisites": [],
   "reward_items": [],
   "title": "Who Speaks for the Mire",
   "turnin": "r20_anchor_046_host",
   "xp": 495
  },
  {
   "copper": 58,
   "description": "Mirefolk Tollkeeper Ush waits in the Whispering Mire Nests southeast from here, demanding coin from everything that floats. Kill Ush and end that claim upon our waters. When the reeds whisper the tale, I want them to remember who stood up for the folk with empty hands.",
   "giver": "r20_anchor_046_host",
   "giver_name": "Enashi Reedvoice",
   "giver_settlement": "Reedvoice Station",
   "id": "whispering_voice_02",
   "min_level": 28,
   "objectives": [
    "kill 1 tollkeeper_ush"
   ],
   "objectives_raw": [
    {
     "count": 1,
     "mobs": [
      "grug_mobs:tollkeeper_ush"
     ],
     "type": "kill"
    }
   ],
   "prerequisites": [
    "whispering_voice_01"
   ],
   "reward_items": [],
   "title": "The River Has No Purse",
   "turnin": "r20_anchor_046_host",
   "xp": 765
  },
  {
   "copper": 6,
   "description": "You have given these waters a tale worth carrying, and I will see that it travels. Go to Tornstandard Hold on Bannerbreak Mesa and speak with Yarra Standardmender. The Throng needs hands like yours where the banners tear, as surely as we needed them among the reeds.",
   "giver": "r20_anchor_046_host",
   "giver_name": "Enashi Reedvoice",
   "giver_settlement": "Reedvoice Station",
